---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="The limits of the educational information on Psychology Blog."
>
  <div class="container narrow section">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Before you read</p><h1>
        Information, with clear limits.
      </h1><p>Last updated 6 November 2026.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>General education</h2><p>
        Psychology Blog shares general educational information about psychology
        and everyday wellbeing. It does not provide medical advice, diagnosis,
        therapy, treatment, or a professional relationship with a reader.
      </p>
      <h2>Your circumstances matter</h2><p>
        An article cannot consider your health, history, relationships, or
        living conditions. An idea that is useful to one person may not fit
        another. You can leave any suggestion that does not feel suitable.
      </p><p>
        For questions about symptoms, treatment, medication, or your personal
        care, speak with an appropriately qualified professional. Do not delay
        seeking care or change prescribed treatment because of an article on
        this site.
      </p>
      <h2>No promise of results</h2><p>
        We do not promise that reading or trying an idea will prevent, improve,
        or resolve a mental health condition. The current articles are sample
        drafts awaiting editorial review. They do not carry a claim of clinical
        review.
      </p>
      <h2>Urgent support</h2><p>
        This website does not monitor requests for help. If you or someone else
        is in immediate danger, contact local emergency services or go to the
        nearest emergency department. See <a href="/get-help/">Get Help</a> for ways
        to find local support.
      </p>
      <h2>References and external links</h2><p>
        Links are offered for further reading. Their presence does not mean an
        external organization endorses this blog. We do not control external
        content, availability, or privacy practices.
      </p>
      <p class="callout">
        This disclaimer is a draft and requires legal review before public
        launch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
